 "equipment_type": "Chiller plant controller (water-cooled chillers, pumps and towers)",
 "applies_to": "Armstrong EE-W10 water-cooled chilled water plant controls; the object list covers up to 3 chillers, 3 chilled water pumps, 3 condenser water pumps and 3 towers.",
 "summary": "The EE-W10 controls a small water-cooled chilled water plant. Its BACnet object list gives plant start/stop, alarm reset, plant load, power and efficiency, chilled and condenser water temperatures and flows, chiller, pump and tower run feedbacks and alarms, valve positions, drive data and Hand/Auto overrides for up to 3 chillers. The same document also lists the Modbus RTU registers.",
 "bacnet_transport": [],
 "firmware": "BACnet communication interface Rev 24.071",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "The data-points sheet titles the table BACnet but does not say whether it is BACnet IP or MS/TP.",
  "Mode objects (AV) use 0 = Not Used, 1 = Hand, 2 = Off, 3 = Auto. Duty/standby, chiller duty and chiller state objects are coded values; the codes are in each point's states.",
  "Hand/Auto BVs and Hand Command BVs, plus the Hand Speed / Hand Position AOs, let the BMS run a valve, pump or fan by hand. Set Lead objects act only when the written value changes.",
  "Units for temperatures, pressures and flows follow the controller's unit setting (the PDF lists the options).",
  "Footnote asterisks after some pump names in the PDF are left off the object names. They mean: for dualArm or Twin pumps, pump numbers 1-5 are the A sides and 6-10 the B sides, and those pumps only report duty or standby because they run in dedicated mode with their chiller.",
  "The PDF table is on pages 9-13. One Reserved AI is left out."
 ],
 "integration": {
  "summary": "The EE-W10 publishes a fixed BACnet object list. Start and stop the plant with BO 1 Remote Start, write the zone setpoint (AV 2), and read BI 1 Plant Status, plant load, chilled water temperatures, plant power and efficiency. Use BO 3 to reset alarms. Per-chiller, per-pump and per-valve alarms, run feedbacks and Hand/Auto overrides are there if the BMS needs more detail.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BO 1",
    "name": "Remote Start",
    "why": "Plant start/stop from the BMS (1 = start)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 2",
    "name": "Zone 1 Setpoint",
    "why": "Zone 1 control setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BO 3",
    "name": "Alarm Reset",
    "why": "Reset plant alarms (positive edge)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 1",
    "name": "Plant Status",
    "why": "Plant on/off status"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 3",
    "name": "Plant Load",
    "why": "Plant cooling load, tons"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 1001",
    "name": "chws Temp",
    "why": "Chilled water supply temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 1002",
    "name": "chwr Temp",
    "why": "Chilled water return temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 2",
    "name": "Total Plant Power Consumption",
    "why": "Total plant power, kW"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 1",
    "name": "Plant Efficiency",
    "why": "Plant efficiency, kW/ton"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 10",
    "name": "Refrigerant Leak Alarm",
    "why": "Refrigerant leak detected"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "BO 1 Remote Start (0 = Stop, 1 = Start) starts and stops the plant from the BMS. The data-points sheet says nothing more about local/remote selection.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "The data-points sheet does not give the device instance, MAC address, baud rate or IP settings; get them from the controller setup."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "BO 3 Alarm Reset acts on a positive edge (0 to 1); write 0 again before the next reset.",
   "Hand/Auto BVs and Hand Command / Hand Speed objects override the plant sequence; leave them in Auto for normal operation.",
   "Mode AVs are coded 0-3 (1 = Hand, 2 = Off, 3 = Auto); writing them takes that equipment out of automatic sequencing.",
   "Set Lead Chiller / Pump objects act only when the value changes, so rewriting the same value does nothing."
  ]
 },
